{"id": "EUVD-2026-24898", "enisaUuid": "c785bf25-f361-3d09-a5a6-b4b97e8f552a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nerofs: set fileio bio failed in short read case\n\nFor file-backed mount, IO requests are handled by vfs_iocb_iter_read().\nHowever, it can be interrupted by SIGKILL, returning the number of\nbytes actually copied. Unused folios in bio are unexpectedly marked\nas uptodate.\n\n  vfs_read\n    filemap_read\n      filemap_get_pages\n        filemap_readahead\n          erofs_fileio_readahead\n            erofs_fileio_rq_submit\n              vfs_iocb_iter_read\n                filemap_read\n                  filemap_get_pages  <= detect signal\n              erofs_fileio_ki_complete  <= set all folios uptodate\n\nThis patch addresses this by setting short read bio with an error\ndirectly.", "datePublished": "2026-04-22T13:54:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T08:20:15", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d1ba7d6b3cd1757b108d7b6856c92ae661d6c323", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5cf3972c8221abdb1b464a14ccf8103d840b9085", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5a5f23ef5431639db1ac3a0b274aef3a84cc413c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eade54040384f54b7fb330e4b0975c5734850b3c"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-31514", "GHSA-mgg3-9x9v-hwxx"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "27b74ed8-b1bc-3201-a16b-e866dd9574a2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ce63cb62d794c98c7631c2296fa845f2a8d0a4a1 <eade54040384f54b7fb330e4b0975c5734850b3c"}, {"id": "2f897c62-039a-30e1-943f-cd2053484a0b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12"}, {"id": "3d63302b-d139-38ce-be04-712e9dfd1946", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19.11"}, {"id": "4b815dfd-b634-3c81-8e8d-d885b2152e70", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ce63cb62d794c98c7631c2296fa845f2a8d0a4a1 <5cf3972c8221abdb1b464a14ccf8103d840b9085"}, {"id": "4f8b9685-6673-3902-b529-23d850169c2b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.80"}, {"id": "5278ab5b-8eb4-3306-8d3f-a343e7aa3b8a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0"}, {"id": "59e37a42-00bf-3893-8755-97bbde817810", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6c1489cb-c4e6-3337-86f8-0d09711690bc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.21"}, {"id": "c8b555db-6d55-39f0-8680-7c2ca144041d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ce63cb62d794c98c7631c2296fa845f2a8d0a4a1 <d1ba7d6b3cd1757b108d7b6856c92ae661d6c323"}, {"id": "da5202c0-2474-3b39-968d-3318f532f960", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ce63cb62d794c98c7631c2296fa845f2a8d0a4a1 <5a5f23ef5431639db1ac3a0b274aef3a84cc413c"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2cfa7754-02ba-3c40-bff6-4fb9a818bebf", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}